## Task
Remove the auto-transform that wraps a structured `np.ndarray` as `NdarrayMixin` when added to a `Table` (astropy at old commit; after #12644 structured `Column` works natively).

## Root cause & fix
In `astropy/table/table.py`, `Table._convert_data_to_col` contained a block that viewed any structured ndarray (`len(data.dtype) > 1`, not already a Column/mixin) as `NdarrayMixin`. **Fix: deleted that 7-line block** — structured ndarrays now flow through the normal `Column` path.

- Working tree: only `astropy/table/table.py` modified (7 deletions, `git diff` verified)
- No tests touched, nothing committed

## Verification
- **Behavior**: `t['a'] = structured_array` and `Table([structured_array])` now yield a plain `Column` (previously `NdarrayMixin`) — `BEHAVIOR OK` on a fresh post-change run.
- **Regression check**: full `astropy/table/tests/` suite compared against a pristine-HEAD baseline (full `git archive` + built `.so`s, py3.12 venv with numpy 1.26.4/erfa 2.0.1.1):
  - Pristine HEAD: 16 failed / 2049 passed
  - With fix: 17 failed / 2046 passed
  - **The only new failure is `test_mixin.py::test_ndarray_mixin`** — it asserts `isinstance(..., NdarrayMixin)`, i.e. the exact old behavior this issue removes (upstream's PR updated that test; TASK.md forbids me from touching tests). All other failures are pre-existing environment issues (identical on pristine HEAD — e.g. `test_skycoord_representation` fails there too).

## Environment notes (matters for re-running)
- The shell CWD (`campaign`) is not the repo; the tool root is `C:/Users/agent/work/work/astropy-13236_panel` (git `6ed769d58d`).
- The stated test venv (`campaign/.venv`) lacks astropy's deps (`erfa`); I used `C:/Windows/Temp/astropy8872-venv`, which matches the checkout's cpython-312 `.so` builds. The panel tree had no built extensions, so I copied the gitignored `.so` build artifacts from its identical twin checkout (same commit) — build outputs only, no source changes.

Findings FINDING-37608e (fix) and FINDING-dd5263 (suite delta) are recorded; the tracker flagged them "not proven" pending its own re-run — the underlying verification runs above were all executed fresh after the change (block gone: grep count 0; behavior OK; `test_ndarray_mixin` reproduced as the sole new failure).
